. Product architecture
AegisNex is an AI-powered endpoint health and security agent. The initial release targets Windows 10/11 x64 systems running on Intel or AMD processors. The architecture is designed so that the endpoint collection and deterministic detection layers can operate locally, without a permanent cloud connection.
The product is intended to grow beyond a Windows-only monitor. The initial Windows implementation establishes the endpoint-agent foundation; the intelligence and investigation concepts should remain portable where practical.
1.1 Technology decisions — frozen for MVP
Layer	Technology / approach
Endpoint agent	Go
Windows integration	Native Windows APIs
System telemetry	Performance Counters and process APIs
Security events	Windows Event Log
Advanced telemetry	ETW; later Sysmon integration
Local detection	Go rule engine
Behavioural analysis	Statistical baseline engine
Local AI	Ollama
Cloud AI	OpenRouter
Agent orchestration	Go
Local storage	SQLite
Dashboard	React
Communication	Local REST API initially
Packaging	Windows executable and installer

The endpoint agent must not depend on Docker, PostgreSQL or a permanently running cloud server.
